      "header": "@@ -62,6 +62,6 @@ describe('MatDivider', () => {",
      "sha256": "674c5634a0baeaedf09c0ebe697c7feabd613da8882bcfa2107a0fcd50938e7f",
      "judgment": "The only hunk replaces two uninitialized boolean fields with false initializers. Complete source confirms the fixture template binds those fields; undefined-to-false is a real test input change. Current list public module/harness imports are retained and hashed in the review. Only this private upstream fixture is excluded; ordinary divider theming and public compatibility are not exempted."
    }
  ],
  "semantics": {
    "kind": "fixture-runtime-default-initialization",
    "before_values": "undefined",
    "after_values": false,
    "emitted_runtime_change": true,
    "ordinary_type_only_cleanup": false
  },
  "decision": "The complete original divider patch initializes the private MatDividerTestComponent vertical and inset fields to false instead of leaving them undefined. This changes emitted runtime values and is not a type-only strictness annotation. The owned package has no such fixture. It does use the stable public MatDividerModule in its list module and MatDividerHarness in its list harness, so divider is reachable and remains subject to peer compatibility. The patch changes no divider implementation, public declaration, selector, style or Sass. Do not copy the private fixture or alter the public dependency to mirror these unrelated private defaults.",
